<section class="case-section">
  <div class="case-section__head"><span class="mono" data-reveal>Context</span><h2 class="display-s" data-split>A card game its players own.</h2></div>
  <div class="case-section__body prose" data-reveal>
    <p>Skyweaver is a free-to-play digital collectible card game where the cards are the players’ to keep, trade and sell. I joined Horizon in 2020 and led the game’s vision through four years of live operation, managing a team of seven junior designers and working shoulder to shoulder with engineering and art.</p>
    <p>Ownership raises the stakes of every design decision. When a card is an asset, balance is a promise, an expansion is a market event, and the economy has to be fair in a way most free-to-play games never have to be.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section">
  <div class="case-section__head"><span class="mono" data-reveal>What I led</span><h2 class="display-s" data-split>Two expansions. Four systems rebuilt.</h2></div>
  <div class="case-section__body" data-reveal>
    <ul>
      <li><span><b>Clash of Inventors &amp; Hexbound Invasion.</b> Co-led both expansions end to end — set design, card design, balance, narrative, and the release beats around them.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Hero Abilities.</b> Gave every hero a signature ability, widening the strategic space without widening the rulebook.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Economy 2.0.</b> Rebuilt how value enters and leaves the game so effort, not spend, is the surest path to power.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Quests 2.0 &amp; Ranked 2.0.</b> Reworked the daily loop and the competitive ladder so the reason to log in and the reason to improve pointed the same way.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>AI adoption across the design team.</b> Introduced AI-assisted prototyping, balance analysis and writing to a team of seven — and taught them to use it well.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<ul class="case-numbers" data-stagger>
  <li class="number"><span class="number__value">+240%</span><span class="number__label">Retention</span></li>
